# Laziness proof: $filter predicate not called for elements beyond what is consumed.
# We filter a Seq whose second element contains an error-trap sentinel.
# [take 1] consumes only the first element. The predicate for the sentinel is never
# called because $filter is lazy — it produces a Seq where each element's predicate
# application is deferred until that element is demanded.
[collect [take 1
    [filter
     [fn [let x] [< x 100]]
     [seq 42 [seq [raise "predicate should not fire"] []]]]]]
